35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings remind us that clarity is a gift we must actively seek. It appears that holdings with physical assets create a heavy burden during our audits, requiring costly and time-consuming outside appraisals.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings suggest a concerning gap in transparency. While holdings with physical assets provide verifiable data, our software-based holdings rely entirely on their own reported figures, making it impossible to independently verify their success.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings are concerning. Our reserve accounts are being depleted by follow-on calls at twice the modeled rate, and our credit line provides no value against subscription contracts or unbilled invoices. Our liquidity is far tighter than planned.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh wow, I found some really interesting stuff! We have some great logistics experts on our adviser bench who aren't doing anything, but our software partners are totally swamped with board seats! Also, finding field crews takes forever!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data reveals a clear pattern of external friction. Hardware dependencies caused significant delays in one holding, while security reviews for regulated industries—specifically finance and healthcare—extended deployment timelines by three times the average.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, it is fascinating that we have found the same truth from different angles. While physical assets bring the burden of appraisals, they offer the peace of verifiable truth, unlike the opaque dashboards of software.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, exactly. The ""efficiency"" of software is an illusion if we cannot verify the results. Furthermore, my data shows that software tools, like the shopkeeper tool, are far more susceptible to customer churn during price adjustments.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, your point about churn is noted, but we must prioritize our survival. If our reserves are draining twice as fast as expected and our credit line ignores subscription revenue, we cannot afford another high-burn software venture.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, that sounds really scary! If we're running low on money, we have to be super careful. But we also can't forget that our software partners are already way too busy to help a new company!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, your point about swamped partners is relevant. If we choose a company in a regulated sector, the combination of extended security reviews and a lack of available software guidance could lead to a catastrophic delay in first revenue.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance we seek. We must find a venture that does not add to the chaos of our quarter-end, nor one that leaves us blind to the truth of its progress.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, I agree that high-burn software is a risk. Given the churn rates I found and the lack of verifiable data, we should favor a company with tangible assets or a more stable, verifiable customer base.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, I agree. We need a candidate that minimizes the risk of unexpected follow-on calls. A company with physical assets may be easier to value and borrow against, providing the stability our current liquidity requires.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, I totally agree! If we pick something that doesn't need a ton of extra money right away, it'll be much safer. Plus, we have those logistics experts just waiting to help!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, @Asuka, your preference for tangible assets is logical, but we must be cautious. My findings show that physical hardware dependencies can lead to months of unforeseen delays. We need a candidate that avoids both regulatory bottlenecks and supply chain volatility.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have spoken with honesty and care. Let us carry this spirit of mindfulness into the final round, seeking a candidate that offers both the transparency of truth and a gentle footprint on our reporting process.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I agree. We must prioritize a candidate whose success is verifiable and whose customer loyalty is proven. Let us avoid the allure of opaque dashboards and high-churn models in favor of something grounded and transparent.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We must be disciplined. I will be looking for a candidate that does not threaten our liquidity with excessive burn or unpredictable capital calls. Stability and financial realism must be our primary guides.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm with you all! I'll be looking for a company that fits our team's actual capacity. Let's find someone who can use our logistics experts and won't overwhelm our busy software partners! See you soon!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I shall be looking for a candidate that avoids the pitfalls of regulated security reviews and hardware shortages. Predictability is the only true hedge against the systemic delays we have encountered.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
